!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = Banked fresh-frozen OSCC samples were obtained from the in collaboration with the Ohlson Research Institute and the Department of Pathology and Laboratory Medicine. This study was reviewed and approved by the Health Research Ethics Board of Alberta – Cancer Committee (reference number: HREBA.CC-16-0644) A subset of samples were then chosen for downstream processing based on tissue quality. OSCC samples were permeabilized enzymatically according to the Visium Protocol CG000240. Samples were then processed using the Visium Spatial Gene Expression Reagent Kit according to the manufacturer’s instructions (10x Genomics, Pleasanton, CA, USA).
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = OSCC samples were permeabilized enzymatically according to the Visium Protocol CG000240. Samples were then processed using the Visium Spatial Gene Expression Reagent Kit according to the manufacturer’s instructions (10x Genomics, Pleasanton, CA, USA).
!Sample_data_processing = All raw FASTQ reads were aligned to Homo_sapiens : GRCh38 reference using the spaceranger count algorithim and quantified through the 10X Genomics space ranger spatial transcriptomics pipeline, with default and recommended parameters. Spaceranger outputs were combined and read depth normalized using the spaceranger aggr function, producing aggregated feature-barcode matrices used in downstream analysis.
!Sample_data_processing = Assembly: Homo_sapiens : GRCh38
!Sample_data_processing = Supplementary files format and content: Filtered feature - barcode HDF5 file output from spaceranger pipeline, Spatial tissue position list CSV, high resolution tissue image as a PNG, scalefactors for tissue positions as a JSON
!Sample_data_processing = Library strategy: Spatial Transcriptomics
